David Goodyear[050301][050301]http://jeffersoniantoo.blogspot.com/[050301]I recently ran into this problem at a music store.  I wanted to buy a sustain pedal for my eletronic keyboard.  I found one I liked and tried to get it rung up.  The clerk asked if I wanted an extended service policy, for half the price of the pedal,...I declined.  He then started asking for my personal information.  I told him he didn't need any of that.  I had the cash out and was ready to pay, but he kept insisting that the register wouldn't let him complete the sale with out the requested information.  I finally said, "Look, I'd like to buy this pedal, but I am paying cash for it and I am not supplying any other information.  Do you want to make a sale or not?"  The clerk replied that he did want to make the sale, but could not without the requested information.  I replied, "Well, I guess I'll have to try elsewhere...", put my money back in my pocket and left the clerk with a very confused look on his face.  I bought a pedal at a different store, for slightly less money, for cash, no questions asked.[050301]03-01-2005 13:01
